Package: com.albrhi.youtube
Name: Albrhi for YouTube (rootless)
Version: 0.1.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Description: A native settings panel for YouTube, in Arabic or English — starting with the truth about your build.
 .
 This is the first release of Albrhi for YouTube and it is deliberately small. It
 adds its own section to YouTube's own settings, and one page inside it that reports
 what the tweak actually finds in your copy of YouTube.
 .
 ▍WHY START HERE
 Downloading from YouTube is not a matter of grabbing a link. YouTube streams
 through a protocol that hands out media in pieces rather than files, and the app
 also carries its own downloader for offline playback. Which of those is reachable
 cannot be read off the app from outside — it has to be measured on a real device,
 on a real video.
 .
 That is what this page does. Play something, open it, and it prints exactly what
 YouTube told the app about that video: every quality, every format, every stream.
 One tap copies the report. Guessing instead of measuring is how weeks get wasted.
 .
 ▍WHAT IS HERE NOW
 A settings section that looks like it shipped with YouTube, full Arabic and English
 with right-to-left layout, and the diagnostics page above.
 .
 ▍WHAT IS NOT HERE YET
 Everything else. No downloads, no ad removal, no player changes. They are being
 built on what this page reports rather than on guesswork, and each will arrive when
 it is verified against a real build instead of assumed.
 .
 Installing this changes nothing about how YouTube plays, looks or behaves.
 .
